{
  "about": [
    "SHARED test cases for every SDK implementation. Each case says: call this method with these",
    "arguments and exactly this must go on the wire - which path, which query parameters, which form",
    "fields (including their encoded values), which file under which field name.",
    "",
    "This is the ONLY thing that catches a mismatch between languages. Each side's own suite only",
    "proves that side agrees with itself; two sides that agree with themselves and disagree with",
    "each other stay green on both. Three real bugs went through exactly that gap - see the top of",
    "`python/orilife/_wire.py`.",
    "",
    "Measurement boundary: these cases pin the point where a method calls `request()`, that is the",
    "MAPPING (path, field names, value encoding). The transport underneath (building multipart,",
    "waiting out a 429, typing errors) is held by each language's own suite. Said so that nobody",
    "reads the green here as 'everything is tested'.",
    "",
    "An uploaded file is written as {\"$file\": \"<name>\"}; each implementation builds it into its own",
    "file type. {\"$single_file\": \"<name>\"} is ONE file NOT wrapped in a list, built the most natural",
    "way for that language - a path string in Python, a file object in JavaScript. The two",
    "constructions differ ON PURPOSE: each language breaks its own way at exactly this spot (Python",
    "iterates a string character by character, JavaScript calls `.map` on something that is not an",
    "array), and the case has to reach both. A case that builds the same input here stays green",
    "under both mutants, which means it tests nothing.",
    "",
    "Values in `fields`/`query` are written as STRINGS because that is the form they travel in."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
